- If a prompt style consistently produces high-quality, accepted content, the system should preserve and refine that approach.
- If certain niches, categories, or visual styles perform better, the system should prioritize them based on available evidence.
- It should compare acceptance rates, rejection rates, production volume, and other relevant metrics over time.
- It should identify workflows that waste credits or repeatedly generate unsuitable content.
- It should measure whether the time and cost required to produce accepted content are decreasing.
