# 11. Content Quality Control and Automated Evaluation

The agent should not blindly accept every generated image or video.

Investigate how to implement a reliable quality-control pipeline that evaluates content before it enters a submission batch.

For images, this could include:

- Resolution and technical specifications.
- Sharpness, artifacts, noise, and upscaling defects.
- Visual coherence and obvious generation errors.
- Composition and commercial usability.
- Duplicate or near-duplicate detection.
- Metadata and keyword quality.

For videos, this could include:

- Resolution, frame rate, duration, and encoding.
- Flickering, visual artifacts, and inconsistent motion.
- Unnatural transitions or malformed objects.
- Unwanted text, logos, or other problematic elements.
- Repeated frames and insufficient visual quality.
- Audio issues when applicable.
- Commercial usability and technical submission requirements.

The actual checks should depend on each platform's current requirements.

Determine which checks can be automated reliably, which require AI-based judgment, and which still require human review.

I want the agent to reject content that is clearly unsuitable and flag uncertain cases instead of pretending to guarantee acceptance.

